  "id": "patch-clamp-technique",
  "term": "patch-clamp technique",
  "definition": "The patch-clamp technique is an electrophysiological method used to record electrical ion currents across a cell membrane. In the whole-cell form described here, it was used to measure calcium-related signals from human atrial muscle cells.",
